# Busy-spin static-check allowlist (T-2672).
# One drift-stable signature per line: <relpath>::<enclosing-fn>::busy-spin
# A `#` starts a comment. fn-name-keyed: survives line moves; a fn RENAME re-fires
# the site (intended re-review). Acknowledges long-poll loops that are SAFE because
# their error path provably EXITS the loop (no re-dispatch → no busy-spin), which the
# grep cannot see from the loop body alone. Each entry cites why.

# cmd_wait: the event.subscribe Err(_) arm does `anyhow::bail!` (returns Err, exits the
# loop) on RPC error — a dead/half-open hub bails immediately, no zero-delay re-dispatch.
# Additionally deadline-bounded at the loop top.
crates/termlink-cli/src/commands/events.rs::cmd_wait::busy-spin

# termlink_request (MCP): the event.subscribe error arm is `Err(e) => return json_err(...)`
# — returns from the fn, exiting the loop. Also deadline-bounded (remaining.is_zero()).
crates/termlink-mcp/src/tools.rs::termlink_request::busy-spin

# termlink_wait (MCP): error arm `Err(e) => return json_err("connection lost: {e}")` —
# returns from the fn, exiting the loop. Also deadline-bounded.
crates/termlink-mcp/src/tools.rs::termlink_wait::busy-spin

# termlink_agent_ask (MCP): error arm `Err(e) => return json_err("connection lost: {e}")`
# — returns from the fn, exiting the loop. Also deadline-bounded.
